CAT = "s66Communication"; SEG = "COM"
Q = [
('Under the USA, the fact that a security is effectively registered means the Administrator has:',
 'Not judged its merits', ['Found the filing accurate', 'Approved its offering price', 'Recommended it to buyers'],
 'USA Section 405 says registration is not a finding that a filing is true or complete, nor approval of the merits of any security, and it is unlawful to tell a buyer otherwise.'),
('An adviser tells a prospect that a strategy will never lose money. This statement is:',
 'Prohibited as a guarantee', ['Allowed if past results back it', 'Allowed with a written disclaimer', 'Allowed for accredited clients'],
 'Promising that a client will not lose, or guaranteeing a result, is a misleading statement and an unethical practice. Past results and disclaimers do not make it lawful.'),
('Under the USA, a guaranteed security is one guaranteed as to payment of:',
 'Principal, interest or dividends', ['Market price on the day of any sale', 'A minimum yearly return', 'Its credit rating'],
 'USA Section 401(e) defines guaranteed as guaranteed as to payment of principal, interest or dividends. Nobody can guarantee a market price or rating.'),
('Under the USA, an advisory contract must generally say the adviser will not be paid based on:',
 'Share of capital gains', ['Hourly rate', 'Percentage of assets managed', 'Flat annual fee'],
 'USA Section 102(c) requires the written contract to bar compensation based on a share of capital gains or appreciation, unless a rule permits it. Asset-based, hourly and flat fees are allowed.'),
('An adviser organized as a partnership must, under its advisory contracts, notify clients of:',
 'A change in its membership', ['A change in its custodian bank', 'A change in its office lease', 'A change in its fiscal year'],
 'The USA and the Advisers Act require an adviser that is a partnership to notify clients of any change in the membership of the partnership within a reasonable time.'),
('Before completing a principal trade with an advisory client, an adviser must:',
 'Disclose in writing, get consent', ['Get verbal approval after the trade', 'Notify the Administrator first', 'Obtain FINRA approval'],
 "USA Section 102(a)(3), modeled on Advisers Act Section 206(3), requires written disclosure of the capacity in which the adviser is acting, and the client's consent, before the transaction is completed."),
('An agent posts static content about a mutual fund on a public social media profile. Under FINRA rules this is:',
 'Retail communication', ['Correspondence', 'Institutional communication', 'Private message'],
 'Static content on a public site available to retail investors is a retail communication and generally needs principal approval before posting. Interactive content is treated like a public appearance.'),
('Business text messages between an agent and clients must be:',
 'Captured and kept by the firm', ['Deleted after 30 days', 'Kept only if a trade results', 'Sent from a personal phone'],
 'SEC Rule 17a-4 requires broker-dealers to preserve business communications, whatever the medium. Off-channel messaging the firm cannot capture breaks the rule.'),
('A broker-dealer must deliver Form CRS to a new retail investor:',
 'By the earliest of an order, a recommendation or account opening', ['By the end of the first month after the account is opened', 'Along with the first quarterly account statement it sends', 'Only after the investor asks the firm for a copy of it'],
 "Under Regulation Best Interest's companion rule, Form CRS is delivered before or at the earliest of a recommendation, an order, or opening an account."),
('Part 2B of Form ADV, the brochure supplement, describes:',
 'Its advisory personnel', ["Firm's fee schedule", "Firm's audited financials", "Firm's ownership chain"],
 'Part 2B gives information about the supervised persons who advise the client, such as education, business experience and disciplinary history. Fees and services are in Part 2A.'),
('Under the Advisers Act, a firm may call itself investment counsel only if:',
 'Its main business is advice', ['It manages over $100 million', 'Its owners are lawyers', 'It is registered in one state'],
 'Advisers Act Section 208(c) limits the name investment counsel to registered advisers whose principal business is giving investment advice and continuous supervisory services.'),
('An advisory contract says the client waives any claim against the adviser for negligence. Such a clause is:',
 'Void as a waiver of the law', ['Allowed if the client signs', 'Allowed for wealthy clients', 'Required by the SEC'],
 'A hedge clause that leads a client to believe she has given up legal rights is misleading, and the Advisers Act and USA void any condition waiving compliance with the law.'),
]
